      "name": "Notifications — Shade",
      "context": "Android only. What Shroud posts to the notification shade (one channel each: Messages, Calls, Contact requests). Drawn by Android in the device's colours. The body is always a fixed line per kind — the server has no text to send. With Show Sender on, the FCM data message carries the sealed name; the app opens it and posts MessagingStyle with the name as title. Off, or before the first unlock after a restart, the title is Shroud. Messages group per chat; tapping opens the chat behind the lock screen. No inline reply in v1 (it would need the history key while locked).",
